      "ts": "20261005_2252",
      "sender_norm": "POLITICO",
      "subject": "EPP puts forward auto package plans",
      "subject_en": "EPP puts forward auto package plans",
      "html": "data/pdfs/20261005_2252_EPP_puts_forward_auto_package_plans.html",
      "pdf": "data/pdfs/20261005_2252_EPP_puts_forward_auto_package_plans.html",
      "summary_en": "The European People's Party is pushing to soften the EU's auto emissions rules, proposing to average standards over five years instead of three and to raise the cap on offsetting emissions with alternative fuels from 3% to 10%. The amendments also widen the zero-emission vehicle definition to include cars running on eligible fuels like biofuels or e-fuels, not just electric vehicles. Green groups and the Socialists and Democrats oppose the changes, arguing such fuels should instead be reserved for harder-to-decarbonize sectors like shipping and aviation.",
      "summary_ja": "欧州人民党(EPP)は、自動車の排出基準を緩和する動きを強めており、基準の平均化期間を3年から5年に延長し、代替燃料による排出相殺の上限を3%から10%に引き上げる修正案を提示した。さらに、ゼロエミッション車の定義を電気自動車だけでなく、バイオ燃料やe-fuelなど「適格燃料」のみで走行する車にも広げることを提案している。環境保護団体や社会民主進歩同盟(S&D)はこれに反対しており、代替燃料は海運や航空など脱炭素化が難しい分野に優先的に使うべきだと主張している。",
